# reindexed: 2026-05-23 (§2 updated: 5 callers not 4; §5 integration.yml + demo-gha rows; §7 completely rewritten for ADR-0009 startup-applied migrations; §10 assets: migration.sql removed; §10 migration-actuation: no install-time step)
# sha-drift: 2026-05-24 (WireMock JVM consolidation cycle 2): source SHA updated in manifest; index content has no stale WireMock.Net prose; no row edits needed

intro | CI/CD Pipelines - outbound view for this repo | rationale | MVP-CI = build+test+package only; no deploy (CR-0010 §3k); CD deferred until Terraform §4 | @docs/ci-cd-pipelines.md#cicd-pipelines--deployment-dashboard
two-docs | Two CI/CD docs - different concerns | rationale | ci-cd-integration.md = inbound; ci-cd-pipelines.md = outbound (this repo's 5 components -> GHCR) | @docs/ci-cd-pipelines.md#1-two-cicd-docs--different-concerns
topology | Topology - five thin callers, one reusable workflow | topology | _build-and-push-image.yml (reusable) + api/fetcher/frontend/gateway.yml callers + demo-gha.yml (CR-0013 5th caller; content-only baked image); build-kind input switches dotnet|static; path-filtered | @docs/ci-cd-pipelines.md#2-topology--five-thin-callers-one-reusable-workflow
topology-component-image | Component -> image -> Dockerfile mapping | reference | 5-row caller-to-image-to-Dockerfile-to-context table: api/fetcher/frontend/gateway + demo-gha (build context = repo root; COPY reaches testing/fixtures/gha/demo/) | @docs/ci-cd-pipelines.md#component--image--dockerfile
triggers | Triggers | contract | push-main, tag-v*, pull_request, workflow_dispatch; PR builds without push (fork-safe) | @docs/ci-cd-pipelines.md#3-triggers
triggers-concurrency | Concurrency model | contract | concurrency=${{github.workflow}}-${{github.ref}} cancel-in-progress:true (CR-0010 §3i) | @docs/ci-cd-pipelines.md#3-triggers
tag-scheme | Tag scheme (Q5) | contract | docker/metadata-action@v5: tag-push -> vX.Y.Z+vX.Y+sha-<7>+latest; main -> sha-<7>+latest; PR -> pr-<N>-sha-<full> (built, not pushed); demo-gha uses identical tag scheme; DASHBOARD_VERSION substitution in release compose pins demo-gha tag to same version as api/fetcher/frontend/gateway | @docs/ci-cd-pipelines.md#4-tag-scheme-q5
quality-gates | Quality gates | contract | 8-row matrix: blocking (backend-format, backend-unit, frontend-unit, mockup-visual); non-blocking artefacts (backend+frontend coverage); not-gated-in-MVP (frontend-lint D3 lock); watching-week-non-blocking->blocking (integration.yml per CR-0012); build+push-only (demo-gha.yml per CR-0013; content-only; no .NET/unit tests) | @docs/ci-cd-pipelines.md#5-quality-gates
caching | Caching | contract | 4 tiers (CR-0010 §3g): NuGet, npm (setup-node built-in), Playwright-browsers, Docker-layers (per-image scope via scope=${{inputs.image-name}}) | @docs/ci-cd-pipelines.md#6-caching
migrations-startup | Migrations - applied at API startup (ADR-0009) | contract | No CI artefact. API host calls Database.Migrate() between app.Build() and app.Run(); idempotent via __EFMigrationsHistory; failure aborts process non-zero before app.Run(). dotnet-ef tool NOT invoked in CI; .config/dotnet-tools.json retained for local-dev contributor migration authoring | @docs/ci-cd-pipelines.md#7-migrations--applied-at-api-startup
migrations-no-artefact | No migration.sql artefact | rationale | Neither api.yml nor release.yml generates migration.sql; emit-migration-artefact machinery retired by ADR-0009. Pre-ADR-0009 releases shipped a 6th migration.sql asset; current installer does not download it | @docs/ci-cd-pipelines.md#7-migrations--applied-at-api-startup
manual-rerun | Manual reruns via workflow_dispatch | how-to | All 5 callers expose workflow_dispatch; no inputs; pushes latest+sha-<7> from main, only sha-<7> from non-default branches | @docs/ci-cd-pipelines.md#8-manual-reruns--workflow_dispatch
version-bump | Bumping a version - tag flow | how-to | git tag vX.Y.Z + git push origin vX.Y.Z; fires all workflows + release.yml; tag scheme event-driven (no workflow edits) | @docs/ci-cd-pipelines.md#9-bumping-a-version--tag-flow
release-pipeline | Release pipeline - v* tag -> release assets | rationale | Separate .github/workflows/release.yml fires on v* tag push; publishes assets the one-liner installer (issue #7, ADR-0009) consumes; runs alongside the 5 component workflows on the same tag push; outbound in the same sense §1 defines | @docs/ci-cd-pipelines.md#10-release-pipeline--v-tag--release-assets
release-asset-visibility | Asset visibility + fetch auth | contract | Repo + GHCR both private; anonymous fetches return 404; transport-layer choice is GitHub CLI (gh); 4-row surface/auth table covers install.ps1+sh download / docker-compose.release.yml / GHCR image pull / release.yml workflow itself; required gh scope union: read:packages | write:packages | admin:packages; gh auth refresh --scopes read:packages prereq | @docs/ci-cd-pipelines.md#asset-visibility--fetch-auth
release-trigger | Release pipeline trigger | contract | push of tag v* (e.g. v1.2.3) -> release.yml creates GitHub Release + attaches assets; does NOT run on push:main, PRs, or workflow_dispatch from non-tag ref; tag push is sole trigger | @docs/ci-cd-pipelines.md#trigger
release-assets-published | Assets published per release | contract | Five assets per vX.Y.Z release (installer refuses missing): docker-compose.release.yml (image refs templated with ${DASHBOARD_VERSION} at publish), install.ps1 + install.sh, uninstall.ps1 + uninstall.sh. Migration actuation is NOT an asset surface — API self-migrates at startup per ADR-0009; migration.sql no longer published (pre-ADR-0009 releases shipped 6th asset) | @docs/ci-cd-pipelines.md#assets-published
release-canonical-asset-url | Canonical asset URL | contract | https://github.com/<owner>/<repo>/releases/download/<tag>/<asset-name>; durable + immutable per-tag; private-repo gated -> gh release download; raw-content URL is fallback only and also private-gated | @docs/ci-cd-pipelines.md#canonical-asset-url
release-migration-actuation | Migration actuation (release-install) | contract | No install-time actuation. API self-migrates on startup per ADR-0009. Installer does NOT: download migration.sql (asset not published); activate --profile migrate (profile + migrations service removed); carry -SkipMigrations/--skip-migrations flag (nothing to skip). Sequence collapses to: db starts (service_healthy) -> api starts (applies pending EF migrations) -> api serves requests | @docs/ci-cd-pipelines.md#migration-actuation
release-notes | Release notes | how-to | release.yml populates GitHub Release body from CHANGELOG.md (when present) plus auto-generated "Install / upgrade" section pointing at canonical asset URLs | @docs/ci-cd-pipelines.md#release-notes
release-cross-refs | Release pipeline cross-references | links | ADR-0009 (migration actuation decision; supersedes ADR-0005) + issue #7 (triggering requirement) + issue #5 + install/install.ps1 §1 (-RealGha / -Empty / -Demo precondition per CR-0013) + ci-cd-integration.md § Anonymous-mode transport + §7 (startup-applied migration contract) + §4 (tag scheme) + architecture.md §8 footnote (API_TOKEN install-time generation) | @docs/ci-cd-pipelines.md#cross-references
ghcr-to-acr | GHCR -> ACR cutover (Q4 deferred) | future | When Terraform §4 lands: change registry input + swap docker/login-action GHCR for azure/login@v2 + docker/login-action ACR (OIDC); tag scheme registry-agnostic | @docs/ci-cd-pipelines.md#11-ghcr--acr-cutover-q4-deferred
troubleshooting | Troubleshooting | troubleshooting | 6-row symptom/cause/fix table: dotnet-format-drift, playwright-cache-miss, docker-layer-cache-cold, GHCR-403-on-fork-PR, frontend-coverage-empty, ng-test-No-provider-for-Browser | @docs/ci-cd-pipelines.md#12-troubleshooting
future-work | Future work | future | 6-row defer/tracking table: dogfooding-notify-hook (D1), frontend-lint ng-lint (D3), GHCR->ACR (Q4), CD-ACA-revision-update (Q11), Trivy/SBOM, branch-protection-requires-CI-green | @docs/ci-cd-pipelines.md#13-future-work
